                <pb facs="1116" n="1002" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860h.51/147: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in the Kingdom of the Serbs, Croats and
                        Slovenes</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-04-21T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 21,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 22—3:22
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>7. I am informed by the Acting Minister of Finance that the Yugoslav Government
                    has practically concluded a loan for $100,000,000 at 8 percent with Blair and
                    Co., of New York; loan to be used to redeem dinar paper currency up to
                    $30,000,000 and the remainder to be used by the Government in the construction
                    of Belgrade-Adriatic and other railways. If the Government decides not to engage
                    upon the construction itself, Blair is to have the construction option.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
